Chapter: BvtPayWhy
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtNpcMove
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 D-10: a refused checkout names the gv-can-pay term that failed (gv-pay-why). On BvtNpcMove's fixture with two Britain
 keepers' actors: 1 one actor on both sides answers "actors", 2 an empty cart between two answers "line count 0", 4
 gv-can-pay refuses both; -1 a fixture that failed.
  bpy-run : CompositeGame -> Text
  bpy-run (owner) = let v = owner.vendor
    in if v.vendor-count < 2 then "fixture"
    else let a = (list-at v.vendors 0).actor
    in let b = (list-at v.vendors 1).actor
    in let same = gv-pay-why v [] a a
    in let empty = gv-pay-why v [] a b
    in let refused = not (gv-can-pay v [] a a) & not (gv-can-pay v [] a b)
    in show ((if text-starts-with same "actors" then 1 else 0) + (if empty == "line count 0" then 2 else 0) + (if refused then 4 else 0)) & " (" & same & "; " & empty & ")"
  bvt-pay-why : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-pay-why (unused) = when bnm-founded 0
    is Err (e) -> bvt-check ("pay why fixture: " & e) False
    is Ok (owner) -> act
      n <- bpy-run owner
      a <- bvt-check ("D-10: a refused checkout names its failing term, code " & n) (text-starts-with n "7 ")
      a
    end
